ute Progressive Weight Loss Syndrome with Constitutional Features: Less likely due to acute haemodynamic presentation overriding metabolic concerns", "Chronic Alcohol Use with Acute Pancreatitis: Pain localization is atypical for pancreatitis", "Acute Appendicitis: Classic presentation would include right lower quadrant pain"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension requiring IV fluid resuscitation", "Shock state with tachycardia and low blood pressure", "Severe localized right upper quadrant pain (10/10) with guarding"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic Emergency with Haemorrhage", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Oral contraceptive use weakly reduces the likelihood of ectopic pregnancy, as it is a protective factor."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Occlusion", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.079, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of chronic liver findings moderately reduces the likelihood of hepatic vein thrombosis, supporting its exclusion as the immediate cause of shock."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Obstruction with Cholangitis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3921905062753913, "posterior": 0.41767414287461613, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Weight loss and acne modestly increase the likelihood of biliary obstruction with cholangitis, given the LR+ of 5.67."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3", "B3.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Acute Pancreatitis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Localized RUQ pain without epigastric involvement strongly rules out acute pancreatitis as the shock mechanism."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Intra-abdominal Vascular Emergency", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.071, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Localized RUQ pain without pulsatile mass or risk factors weakly disfavors intra-abdominal vascular emergencies as the shock mechanism."]}, "kb_pancreatic": {"id": "kb_pancreatic", "label": "pancreatic", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.0, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Ruptured Ectopic Pregnancy", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Ruptured Hemorrhagic Ovarian Cyst", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of pelvic exam abnormalities weakly reduces likelihood of ovarian cyst rupture as a hemorrhagic source."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Placental Abruption (if pregnancy confirmed)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.006, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Alcohol-related coagulopathy is a more plausible hemorrhage mechanism than placental abruption given absence of confirmed pregnancy."]}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Choledocholithiasis with Acute Cholangitis", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.287, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of jaundice and cholangitis signs moderately contradicts choledocholithiasis with cholangitis, despite weight loss and RUQ pain."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "Cholangiocarcinoma with Obstructive Jaundice", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.092, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of obstructive jaundice weakens cholangiocarcinoma as a diagnosis, though weight loss remains a non-specific marker."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma with Ampullary Obstruction", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.008, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Localized RUQ pain strongly contradicts the diffuse presentation typical of pancreatic adenocarcinoma."]}, "B3.4": {"id": "B3.4", "label": "Biliary Strictures (Inflammatory/Post-Surgical)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.031, "danger": 0.65, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": [], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's sudden right upper quadrant pain exacerbation during exercise and hypotension support a vascular emergency as the shock mechanism?", "summary": "Acute RUQ pain and hypotension during exertion provide weak support for a vascular emergency, but absence of pulsatile mass or risk factors limits this association."}, {"t": 3, "type": "SAFETY_ENSURE", "content": "Does the absence of chronic liver findings (ascites, jaundice, spider angiomas) in a patient with acute shock rule out hepatic vein thrombosis as a life-threatening diagnosis?", "summary": "Absence of chronic liver findings moderately reduces the likelihood of hepatic vein thrombosis, supporting its exclusion as the immediate cause of shock."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of jaundice, fever, and light-colored stools in the vignette sufficiently contradict choledocholithiasis with acute cholangitis as the diagnosis?", "summary": "Lack of jaundice and cholangitis signs moderately contradicts choledocholithiasis with cholangitis, despite weight loss and RUQ pain."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of obstructive jaundice and chronic liver findings in the vignette significantly weaken the likelihood of cholangiocarcinoma with biliary obstruction?", "summary": "Absence of obstructive jaundice weakens cholangiocarcinoma as a diagnosis, though weight loss remains a non-specific marker."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's localized RUQ pain and absence of pulsatile abdominal mass or prior vascular risk factors disfavor intra-abdominal vascular emergencies as a shock mechanism?", "summary": "Localized RUQ pain without pulsatile mass or risk factors weakly disfavors intra-abdominal vascular emergencies as the shock mechanism."}, {"t": 4, "type": "SAFETY_ENSURE", "content": "Does the absence of chronic liver findings (ascites, jaundice, spider angiomas) in the vignette sufficiently rule out hepatic vein thrombosis as a life-threatening diagnosis?", "summary": "The absence of chronic liver findings (ascites, jaundice, spider angiomas) in a patient with acute shock weakly reduces the likelihood of hepatic vein thrombosis as the immediate cause of hypotension."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.32], ["B3.1", 0.219], ["B2", 0.124]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.392], ["B3.1", 0.269], ["B2", 0.106]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.418], ["B3.1", 0.287], ["B3.2", 0.092]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Hypotension (80/40 mmHg) and tachycardia (110/minute) indicate shock, a major haemodynamic instability requiring immediate intervention.", "required_actions": ["Continue IV fluid resuscitation", "Assess for sources of haemorrhage (e.g., ectopic pregnancy via urgent imaging or hCG quantification)", "Monitor urine output and consider vasopressors if hypotension persists"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Emergency override is active due to shock (hypotension/tachycardia), but dangerous alternatives (B1.1 ruptured ectopic pregnancy, B2 hepatic vascular occlusion) remain unresolved. Tree depth (2) is below max allowed (3), and the leading branch (B3.1) has insufficient posterior (0.287) to justify stopping. Further exploration is needed to confirm or exclude life-threatening causes."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.45, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "SAFETY_ENSURE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.28650069375056125, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Portal vein thrombosis', 'Hepatic vein thrombosis', 'Acute abdominal pain', 'Abdominal discomfort', 'Acute pancreatitis', 'Pancreatic adenocarcinoma'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.364}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B3.1", "label": "Choledocholithiasis with Acute Cholangitis", "posterior": 0.287, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 1}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 2, "disconfirming": 2, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Lack of jaundice and cholangitis signs moderately contradicts choledocholithiasis with cholangitis, despite weight loss…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "refute"}, {"t